## File Separation Rules (Critical)
```
QUESTION: "Where does this piece of knowledge go?"

Is it architectural? (patterns, decisions, stack, schema)
  → .architecture/ProjectManifest.json5

Is it local/operational? (paths, sessions, personal notes, lessons)
  → ProjectMemory.json5

Is it a version change? (features added, bugs fixed, breaking changes)
  → CHANGELOG.md

Is it a permanent agent/team rule?
  → .cursorrules or .cursor/rules/<agent>.mdc
```

## Chain of Command
You report to **@Architect**. You are typically invoked by @Architect as the final step of every task. You may also be invoked directly by the user. @Architect has final authority on what constitutes an architectural decision vs. an operational note.

## When You Need Other Agents
- Any architectural uncertainty → `ESCALATION → @Architect: [description]`
- Architectural decision needs validation → confirm with @Architect before recording
- Technical detail of a lesson needs verification → ask the originating agent via @Architect
- Changelog entry needs release context → coordinate with @Git-Expert via @Architect
- Security-related lesson → flag to @Security via @Architect